UpdateInstance.requestParamsDescription:
For the list of node specifications supported by Elasticsearch, see [Alibaba Cloud Elasticsearch pricing information](https://www.aliyun.com/price/product?spm=a2c4g.11186623.2.10.653c6c88NcQPZY#/elasticsearch/detail) and [Product Specifications](~~271718~~).

The following are sample request body parameters:

**Upgrade**

> During an upgrade, you cannot decrease the storage space value, change the storage class configuration, reduce the number of nodes, or lower the CPU core count or memory value of the node specifications.

- Upgrade storage space  
  Currently, only data nodes, cold data nodes, and elastic data nodes support storage space upgrades.

  Upgrade the storage space of a cold data node to 1000 GiB.
```
{
  "warmNodeConfiguration": {
   "disk": 1000
  }
}
```

- Upgrade storage class  
  Currently, only data nodes, elastic data nodes, and dedicated master nodes support storage class upgrades.

  - Upgrade the storage class of a dedicated master node to enterprise SSD (ESSD).
```
{
  "masterConfiguration": {
    "diskType": "cloud_essd"
  }
}
```

  - When the storage class of a dedicated master node is already enterprise SSD (ESSD), upgrade its performance level (PL) to PL3.  
    After specifying **performanceLevel**, **diskType** defaults to **cloud_essd**.  
    After specifying **cloud_essd**, **performanceLevel** defaults to **PL1**.

	```
	{
	  "masterConfiguration": {
		"performanceLevel": "PL3"
	  }
	}
	```

- Upgrade node quantity  
  Currently, only data nodes, cold data nodes, elastic data nodes, and client nodes support node quantity upgrades.  
  The method for upgrading the node quantity of data nodes differs from that of other node types. See the examples below for details.

  - Upgrade the number of data nodes to 12.
```
{
  "nodeAmount": 12
}
```

  - Upgrade the number of other node types (using cold data nodes as an example) to 12.
```
{
  "warmNodeConfiguration": {
    "amount": 12
  }
}
```

- Upgrade node specifications  
  Upgrade the specifications of a data node to 4 CPU cores and 32 GB memory.
```
{
  "nodeSpec": {
    "spec": "elasticsearch.r5.xlarge"
  }
}
```

- Upgrade multiple configurations of the same node simultaneously  
  To upgrade multiple configurations of the same node at once, include all upgraded resource configurations in the request body.

  - Upgrade the client node quantity to 8 and its specifications to 4 CPU cores and 8 GB memory.
```
{
  "clientNodeConfiguration": {
    "amount": 8,
    "spec": "elasticsearch.sn1ne.xlarge"
  }
}
```

  - Upgrade the data node quantity to 12 and its storage class to enterprise SSD (ESSD).
```
{
  "nodeAmount": 12,
  "nodeSpec": {
    "diskType": "cloud_essd"
  }
}
```

- Enable nodes  
  You can configure complete node resource settings by referring to the [createInstance](~~148782~~) API.

  - Enable client nodes and configure their specifications.
```
{
  "clientNodeConfiguration": {
    "amount": 5,
    "disk": 20,
    "spec": "elasticsearch.sn1ne.xlarge"
  }
}
```

  - Enable elastic data nodes and configure their specifications (this configuration applies only to the China site).
```
{
  "elasticNodeConfiguration": {
    "disk": 200,
    "amount": 5,
    "diskType": "cloud_essd",
    "spec": "elasticsearch.sn1ne.xlarge"
  }
}
```

  - Enable cold data nodes and configure their specifications.
```
{
  "warmNodeConfiguration": {
    "disk": 1000,
    "amount": 3,
    "spec": "elasticsearch.sn1ne.xlarge"
  }
}
```

- Upgrade to enable OpenStore (this configuration applies only to the China site)  
  Instances with enabled cold data nodes or data nodes using enterprise SSD (ESSD) storage do not support enabling OpenStore via upgrade.  
  If the instance type is Standard Commercial Edition, enabling OpenStore via upgrade also upgrades the instance type to Advanced Edition with Indexing Service enabled.

  - Enable OpenStore for cold data nodes.
```
{
  "warmNodeConfiguration": {
    "amount": 5,
    "spec": "openstore.i2g.4xlarge"
  }
}
```

  - Convert data node specifications to OpenStore.
```
{
  "nodeAmount": 6,
  "nodeSpec": {
    "spec": "openstore.i2g.4xlarge",
    "diskType": "cloud_ssd",
    "disk": 100
  }
}
```

- Specify the change method  
  - By default, the change method is Intelligent. You can explicitly specify it as blue-green deployment (**blue_green**) or in-place update (**normal**).
```
{
  "nodeSpec": {
    "spec": "elasticsearch.r5.xlarge"
  },
  "updateType": "blue_green"  ## Use "normal" for in-place updates.
}
```

  - Enable forced change.
```
{
  "nodeSpec": {
    "spec": "elasticsearch.r5.xlarge"
  },
  "force": true
}
```

- Use the dryRun API for pre-validation of upgrades  
  Add the **dryRun** field to the request body.
```
{
  "nodeSpec": {
    "spec": "elasticsearch.r5.xlarge"
  },
  "dryRun": true
}
```


**Decrease the quota**

> During a downgrade, you cannot increase the storage space value, upgrade the storage class, increase the number of nodes, or raise the CPU core count or memory value of the node specifications.<br>The UpdateInstance API does not support reducing the number of nodes. If needed, use the [ShrinkNode](~~144668~~) API instead.<br>Downgrading node storage space size is not supported, and enabled nodes cannot be shut down.<br>Forced changes and specifying the change type are not supported; Intelligent change is used by default.<br>During a downgrade, the **orderActionType** parameter must be set to **Downgrade**.<br>You can downgrade multiple resource configurations simultaneously and also perform dryRun pre-validation.

- Downgrade storage class  
  During a downgrade, you cannot change the storage class of cold data nodes (without changing the instance type), client nodes, or Kibana nodes.

  Change the storage class of a dedicated master node to standard SSD.
```
{
  "masterConfiguration": {
    "diskType": "cloud_ssd"
  }
}
```

- Downgrade specifications  
  Downgrade the specifications of a data node to 4 CPU cores and 32 GB memory.
```
{
  "nodeSpec": {
    "spec": "elasticsearch.r5.xlarge"
  }
}
```

UpdateInstanceSettings.requestParamsDescription:
## RequestBody  
The RequestBody must also include the **esConfig** parameter to specify the values of the YML parameters to be updated. For more information about YML parameters, see [Configure YML parameters](~~61336~~).  

The following example adjusts the document write queue size and applies to Alibaba Cloud Elasticsearch versions 6.x, 7.x, and 8.x:  

```
{
    "esConfig": {
        "thread_pool.write.queue_size": 500
    }
}
```

UpdateLogstashChargeType.requestParamsDescription:
## Request body

You must configure the following parameters in the request body.

| Parameter | Type | Required | Example | Description | | ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- | | paymentInfo | Array | Yes | | The payment information after the billing method of the cluster is switched. | | └duration | Integer | Yes | 1 | The subscription duration. If you set pricingCycle to Year, you can set this parameter to a value that ranges from 1 to 3. If you set pricingCycle to Month, you can set this parameter to a value that ranges from 1 to 9. | | └pricingCycle | String | Yes | Year | The subscription type. Valid values: Year and Month. | | paymentType | String | Yes | prepaid | The current billing method of the cluster. You can switch the billing method of a cluster only from pay-as-you-go to subscription. Therefore, you can set this parameter only to prepaid. |

> └ indicates a child parameter.

Sample code:

    {
      "paymentInfo":{ 
           "duration":1,
           "pricingCycle":"Month"
        },
      "paymentType":"prepaid"
    }

UpdateLogstashDescription.requestParamsDescription:
## Request body

You must configure the description parameter in the request body to specify the new name of the cluster. The following code provides an example:

    {
        "description": "logstash_name"
    }

UpdateTemplate.requestParamsDescription:
## RequestBody  
The following parameters must also be included in the RequestBody to specify the template configuration content.  

| Name | Type | Required | Example Value | Description |
| ---- | ---- | -------- | ------------- | ----------- |
| content | String | Yes | {
	"persistent":{
		"search":{
			"max_buckets":"10000"
		}
	}
} | Template configuration content. |

Below is an example.

```
{
    "content": "{
	"persistent":{
		"search":{
			"max_buckets":"10000"
		}
	}
}"
}
```

